  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "xmlTextReaderRemoveID",
    "file": "libxml2/xmlreader.c",
    "description": "Double-free of an xml:id attribute name occurs due to ownership confusion between the ID table entry and attribute teardown. In xmlTextReaderRemoveID, when removing an ID-backed attribute during streaming node cleanup, the code assigns id->name = attr->name and id->attr = NULL. Later, xmlTextReaderFreeProp frees cur->name (the same pointer), and at reader/document destruction xmlTextReaderFreeIDTable -> xmlFreeID frees id->name again, causing the ASan double-free. Crash manifests in xmlFreeID during xmlTextReaderFreeDoc/xmlFreeTextReader, but root cause is pointer aliasing introduced in xmlTextReaderRemoveID.",
    "conditions": "Triggered in xml reader fuzz harness with a document containing an ID attribute (here xml:id=\"\") on a node that gets freed incrementally by xmlTextReaderRead before final reader teardown. Data flow: parser creates attribute name/value -> attribute recognized as ID -> xmlTextReaderFreeProp calls xmlTextReaderRemoveID during node cleanup -> id entry keeps borrowed attr->name pointer -> attribute free releases that name -> later xmlFreeTextReader frees doc IDs table and xmlFreeID frees id->name again. Requires an ID table entry tied to an attribute being removed before doc ID table destruction."
  },
